      <section class="legal-section" id="analytics">
        <span class="legal-section-number">03</span>
        <h2 class="legal-section-title">Google Analytics 4</h2>
        <div class="legal-section-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <p>
          Our website uses <strong>Google Analytics 4 (GA4)</strong>, a audience
          analytics service provided by Google LLC. GA4 allows us to understand
          how our visitors use our website, identify the most visited pages, and
          know the geographical origin of our audience.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>What GA4 measures concretely for us&nbsp;:</strong>
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>The number of visits and unique visitors on the website</li>
          <li>The pages consulted and the navigation path</li>
          <li>The country of origin of the visitors</li>
          <li>The devices and browsers used</li>
          <li>
            The traffic sources (Google, social networks, direct access, etc.)
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          <strong>IP Address Anonymization&nbsp;:</strong> Google Analytics 4
          automatically anonymizes IP addresses before storing them. Your full
          IP address is never stored or transmitted to Google.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>GA4 Identifiers&nbsp;:</strong> GA4 uses an anonymous client
          identifier stored in a cookie (see our
          <a href="/{{ lang }}/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>) to
          distinguish sessions without personally identifying you.
        </p>

        <p>
          Google acts as a <strong>data processor</strong> for our analytics
          data. The processing conditions are governed by Google's
          <em>Data Processing Terms</em> and the European Commission's
          Type-Européennes de Clauses Contractuelles.
        </p>

        <p>
          For more information about Google's privacy policy:&nbsp;:
          <a
            href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >policies.google.com/privacy</a
          >.
        </p>

        <p>
          To disable GA4 tracking &nbsp;:
          <a
            href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Module to disable Google Analytics.</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section" id="base-legale">
        <span class="legal-section-number">04</span>
        <h2 class="legal-section-title">Legal Basis for Data Processing</h2>
        <div class="legal-section-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <p>
          The processing of your data via Google Analytics 4 is based on your
          <strong>consent</strong> (article 6.1.a of the GDPR), obtained through
          our cookie management banner during your first visit. visita.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you have not given your consent for the activation of the
          analytical cookies, no data is transmitted to Google Analytics.
        </p>
        <p>
          The data provided through the contact form (if applicable) is
          processed in virtue of our
          <strong>legitimate interest</strong> in responding to your inquiries
          (article 6.1.f of the GDPR).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section" id="conservation">
        <span class="legal-section-number">05</span>
        <h2 class="legal-section-title">Period of Conservation</h2>
        <div class="legal-section-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <p>
          The data collected through Google Analytics 4 is retained according to
          the following parameters:&nbsp;:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>User and Event Data (GA4)&nbsp;:</strong> 14 months
            (parameter configured in our GA4 property; minimum period
            recommended by Google for annual trend analysis).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>GA4 Cookies (_ga)&nbsp;:</strong> 2 years from the last
            visit.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Agregated Statistical Data&nbsp;:</strong> the aggregated
            reports (number of visits, source country, etc.) may be retained
            without time limit, as they do not contain any personal data.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section" id="transferts">
        <span class="legal-section-number">06</span>
        <h2 class="legal-section-title">International Transfers</h2>
        <div class="legal-section-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <p>
          Google Analytics 4 may transfer data to Google LLC's servers, located
          in the
          <strong>United States</strong>. These transfers are regulated by the
          <strong>Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs)</strong> adopted by the
          European Commission, in accordance with Article 46 of the GDPR.
        </p>
        <p>
          Google LLC has obtained certification under the Datos UE-EE. UU. (<em
            >EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework</em
          >).
        </p>
      </section>

